1
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,020
Doctor's log.

2
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:48,520
It's day 243 in this...

3
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:51,150
portobello purgatory.

4
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:54,030
My only companion 
is a rock I named Stone.

5
00:01:56,780 --> 00:02:00,700
The question is, 
for whom am I narrating this?

6
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:06,170
<i>It seems I've become a featured 
player in the theater of the absurd.</i>

7
00:02:06,290 --> 00:02:09,340
<i>Marooned in deep space 
by that wretched blue rodent.</i>

8
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:11,210
<i>But it's all good,</i>

9
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,840
<i>thanks to a breathable atmosphere 
and my supreme intellect,</i>

10
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:17,300
<i>sharpened against the only 
competitor savvy enough to bring it.</i>

11
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:19,760
Chanterelle to d4. Mmm.

12
00:02:19,890 --> 00:02:23,180
<i>I've been striving to make fungi 
into a functional drink of choice...</i>

13
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:24,770
Mushroom coffee.

14
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:29,230
<i>With limited...</i>

15
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,570
<i>limited...</i>

16
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,030
<i>limited...</i>

17
00:02:35,610 --> 00:02:37,070
<i>success.</i>

18
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,790
<i>But today, day 243,</i>

19
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:46,250
<i>has brought a new optimism 
to my most pressing endeavor...</i>

20
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:51,380
<i>Planetus exodus to returnicus 
and kick blue butticus.</i>

21
00:02:58,090 --> 00:02:59,760
If my calculations are correct,

22
00:02:59,890 --> 00:03:03,720
and there's no reason to say 
"if" because they always are...

23
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:08,100
this quill is going to power 
my masterpiece.

24
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:11,610
Let's light this candle...

25
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:16,200
and see who comes 
a-knockin'.

26
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,140
Greetings!

27
00:04:28,850 --> 00:04:31,310
<i>Klaatu barada nikto.</i>

28
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,530
Agent Stone? Now!

29
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:54,710
Thank you, Stone.

30
00:04:56,300 --> 00:05:01,430
It's time to say goodbye to 
this piece-of-shiitake planet!

31
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:12,600
Huh?

32
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:28,410
Where did you get that?

33
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:34,790
From a little blue menace 
on the planet called Earth.

34
00:05:37,250 --> 00:05:39,630
I'd be happy 
to show you the way.

35
00:05:48,350 --> 00:05:52,270
How excited are you, 
going to Hawaii with me? Oh, Hawaii.

36
00:05:52,430 --> 00:05:54,440
Oh, yeah!

37
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:56,190
Wow.

38
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:59,190
Welcome to Sonic Air, 
the fastest way to travel.

39
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:01,690
Now boarding groups one and two.

40
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:04,280
Oh!

41
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,280
Sonic, this is so fun!

42
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:06,410
There we go.

43
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:08,580
Okay, you're free to go. 
Enjoy your trip.

44
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,040
Bye-bye now.

45
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,700
Okay.

46
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,460
Okay, use this one 
to get back home.

47
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,210
Oh!

48
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:16,710
All right, we're off.

49
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:17,960
Miss you already! Okay?

50
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:19,960
Have fun at Rachel's wedding!

51
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,090
Let's do this.

52
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:29,220
<i>♪ Na-na-na-na ♪</i>

53
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:30,720
<i>♪ Na-na-na-na ♪</i>

54
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,890
<i>♪ Here comes the hotstepper 
Murderer ♪</i>

55
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:35,230
<i>♪ I'm the lyrical gangster 
Murderer ♪</i>

56
00:06:35,350 --> 00:06:37,190
<i>♪ Pick up the crew in-a de area 
Murderer ♪</i>

57
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:41,070
<i>♪ It's how we do it, man ♪</i>

58
00:06:41,230 --> 00:06:42,690
Whoo-hoo!

59
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,240
<i>♪ Na-na-na-na 
Na-na-na, na-na-na ♪</i>

60
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,070
<i>♪ Na-na-na-nah ♪</i>

61
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,740
<i>♪ Yeah, man ♪</i>

62
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:50,780
<i>♪ It's how we do it ♪</i>

63
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:54,660
<i>♪ Na-na-na-na 
Na-na-na, na-na-na ♪</i>

64
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:57,080
<i>♪ Na-na-na-nah ♪</i>

65
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,230
If these readings 
are accurate, he's here.

66
00:07:15,350 --> 00:07:16,390
I found him!

67
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,850
I just hope I'm not too late.

68
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:38,120
Hmm. He's close.

69
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,790
I just need a way to reach 
him without being spotted.

70
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:45,340
Standard human transport. 
Perfect.

71
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,420
<i>♪ This is how we do it ♪</i>

72
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,470
<i>♪ This is how we do it ♪</i>

73
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,970
<i>♪ It's Friday night ♪</i>

74
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,390
Uh-oh.

75
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,100
Oh, boy.

76
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:05,480
<i>Aloha!</i>

77
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:07,650
<i>- How's it going, bud? 
- Oh, you know.</i>

78
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:10,780
Just a quiet night at home, 
settling in with a good book.

79
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:12,030
<i>And you? What's up with you?</i>

80
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,830
I was just calling 
to say we're here.

81
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:14,490
Don't worry.

82
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:17,330
Everything here 
is completely normal.

83
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,710
Uh-huh. Night, bud.

84
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:25,710
All right, Ozzy, 
it's movie night at Casa de Sonic,

85
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:27,050
and it's your turn to pick.

86
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:29,420
<i>But I am not watching 
Snow Dogs again.</i>

87
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,850
Blackout!

88
00:08:33,970 --> 00:08:37,180
Ozzy!

89
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:39,890
Oh, sorry, buddy. 
Everything's okay.

90
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:42,060
Whoa!

91
00:08:46,110 --> 00:08:50,490
Uh, excuse me. 
We did not order a poltergeist.

92
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:11,840
Eggman?

93
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:18,520
Hello, hedgehog.

94
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,180
Did you miss me?

95
00:09:22,230 --> 00:09:23,850
I don't know how you got back,

96
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:26,650
but you made 
a big mistake coming here.

97
00:09:26,770 --> 00:09:29,990
<i>Au contraire, mon frère.</i>

98
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:32,400
The mistake 
was thinking you'd won.

99
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:35,030
But that was just a prelude, 
an hors d'oeuvre,

100
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,450
an aperitif, an amuse-bouche.

101
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,740
I get it.

102
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:41,830
I don't think you do.

103
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,670
But you're about to.

104
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:46,670
And so will that idiot 
sheriff and his wife.

105
00:09:49,090 --> 00:09:50,960
And your little dog too!

106
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:10,940
Pitiful.

107
00:10:11,070 --> 00:10:14,030
What? Who are you?

108
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:18,160
Where are my manners?

109
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:21,910
Sonic, meet Knuckles.

110
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,160
My new BFFAE.

111
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:27,540
Bestest friend forever and ever!

112
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:30,920
Look, Robotnik, I don't care 
who you brought to help you.

113
00:10:31,050 --> 00:10:32,840
You're never going 
to get my power.

114
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,590
Do I look like 
I need your power?

115
00:10:45,890 --> 00:10:49,610
So nice when diabolical evil 
lives up to the hype.

116
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,440
Where is it?

117
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:57,780
Oh, you want it? Here it comes.

118
00:10:57,910 --> 00:11:01,080
I was expecting more of you.

119
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,620
You're unskilled.

120
00:11:03,450 --> 00:11:04,500
Untrained.

121
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:09,710
You forgot one. Unstoppable.

122
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:39,070
It is my destiny to do 
what my ancestors could not...

123
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:43,740
To restore the ultimate power 
to the home of my people.

124
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:45,620
Ultimate power?

125
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:48,080
I don't know 
what you're talking about.

126
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:49,330
You've got the wrong guy.

127
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:51,540
Ultimate power?

128
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:54,750
Now you speak-ee my language.

129
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:07,680
Come on. Get in! 
I'm on your side.

130
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,690
I'm sorry. Who are you?

131
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:12,650
You know what? 
It doesn't matter.

132
00:12:15,150 --> 00:12:17,070
Get us out of here! 
Go, go, go!

133
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:25,200
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

134
00:12:25,330 --> 00:12:26,870
Whoa!

135
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,590
What is going on? 
Robotnik's back?

136
00:12:33,710 --> 00:12:36,000
And who is Clifford 
the Big Red Rage Monster?

137
00:12:36,170 --> 00:12:38,800
That's Knuckles, 
the last of the Echidnas

138
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:41,130
and the most dangerous warrior 
in the galaxy.

139
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:43,470
He's obsessed with finding 
the Master Emerald.

140
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,810
Are you serious? 
The Master Emerald?

141
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:47,560
That's just a bedtime story.

142
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,100
Well, he believes it's real.

143
00:12:49,230 --> 00:12:51,770
And he must think 
you're the key to finding it.

144
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,520
Red light! Give me the wheel!

145
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,730
Hey, what are you... 
Move your foot.

146
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,960
Just let me... Come on! 
What are you doing?

147
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:34,060
We're flying.

148
00:13:45,570 --> 00:13:50,040
Foxy move.

149
00:13:51,370 --> 00:13:53,250
You want something done right...

150
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:57,880
You have to hire someone 
you can push around.

151
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:00,710
All caps.

152
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:17,020
<i>♪ I waited till I saw the sun ♪</i>

153
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:19,070
<i>♪ I don't know why 
I didn't come ♪</i>

154
00:14:19,190 --> 00:14:20,650
Doctor,

155
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:22,650
where are you?

156
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:30,580
Freak.

157
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:40,380
Oh, I, uh... I'm sorry, folks.

158
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:43,090
Uh, I have to close early. 
Everybody out!

159
00:14:43,210 --> 00:14:46,430
Everybody out. Thank you 
for visiting the Mean Bean.

160
00:14:46,550 --> 00:14:48,800
All right, good night. 
Good night.

161
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:08,990
He's back.

162
00:15:10,530 --> 00:15:13,120
He's back!

163
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:09,760
That's more like it.

164
00:16:10,510 --> 00:16:13,640
I've been re-hatched!

165
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:29,400
So, my massively 
metacarpaled friend,

166
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:32,570
you mentioned...

167
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,660
Ultimate power.

168
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:35,790
Back at the house?

169
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:37,500
The Master Emerald?

170
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:39,160
It does not concern you.

171
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:41,920
I got you off that planet and 
you brought me to the hedgehog.

172
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:44,040
We have no more use 
for each other.

173
00:16:44,210 --> 00:16:46,380
Well, I hate to be 
a contrarian, but...

174
00:16:47,590 --> 00:16:48,920
I think we might.

175
00:16:50,470 --> 00:16:52,390
You think these machines 
are a match for me?

176
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:54,640
Oh, they are stairs.

177
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:04,560
You see, Earth is my turf, G.

178
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:07,440
If you don't know how to floss, 
you'll be lost without me.

179
00:17:07,570 --> 00:17:10,150
I understand nothing 
of what you just said.

180
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:15,030
I help you retrieve the Emerald, 
and you use it to...

181
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:21,040
destroy the hedgehog!

182
00:17:21,210 --> 00:17:23,290
You're suggesting an alliance.

183
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:27,750
Around here we simply 
grip each other's hands tightly.

184
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:31,380
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

185
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:36,470
You truculent space bumpkin!

186
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,890
You've crushed my favorite hand!

187
00:17:39,020 --> 00:17:41,560
Really? My hand is uninjured.

188
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:42,730
Ugh.

189
00:17:42,850 --> 00:17:44,900
But I'm now convinced 
of your commitment.

190
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:46,730
"Oh, goody,"

191
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:50,570
he exclaimed, 
while he reset two of his knuckles.

192
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:52,900
I'm...

193
00:17:53,070 --> 00:17:58,240
delighted to be 
on the same team.

194
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,500
Road trip!

195
00:18:07,630 --> 00:18:10,460
I'll let you stick your 
nose out the window.

196
00:18:10,670 --> 00:18:12,170
According to this map,

197
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,800
the first clue is in Siberia.

198
00:18:13,930 --> 00:18:16,300
It's a compass that 
will lead to the Emerald.

199
00:18:16,430 --> 00:18:19,390
And with Knuckles already here, 
it's a race.

200
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,430
We're gonna get there first.

201
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:29,270
<i>♪ Me and you 
Maybe sunshine, maybe rain ♪</i>

202
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:40,120
Doctor. It's really you.

203
00:18:40,830 --> 00:18:42,830
You look different.

204
00:18:42,950 --> 00:18:45,960
Papa's got a brand new 'stache.

205
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:47,880
Ha!

206
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:50,460
I knew it. I knew it!

207
00:18:50,590 --> 00:18:52,260
I knew you'd come back, sir.

208
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:55,800
I never stopped steaming 
your Austrian goat's milk.

209
00:19:00,850 --> 00:19:02,350
Could use some mushroom.

210
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:05,100
You brought something.

211
00:19:05,230 --> 00:19:09,060
Some kind of, uh, 
space porcupine.

212
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:12,150
Porcupine? I am an Echidna!

213
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,070
Welcome to the team.

214
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:22,830
That means he trusts you, Stone.

215
00:19:22,950 --> 00:19:25,660
Now let's renovate this dump!

216
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:28,960
Latte with steamed 
Austrian goat milk!

217
00:19:37,630 --> 00:19:42,140
"Just chilling. Watching TV."

218
00:19:42,310 --> 00:19:42,680
Dot, dot, dot.

219
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:45,060
Dot, dot, dot.

220
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:48,310
Dot, dot, dot.

221
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:50,150
Doctor,

222
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:53,650
why are we working 
with this imbecile?

223
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:59,280
Because that simpleminded space trash 
is the key to something extraordinary.

224
00:19:59,410 --> 00:20:02,330
Something to help you 
get revenge on the hedgehog.

225
00:20:02,450 --> 00:20:04,160
Think bigger, Stone.

226
00:20:04,290 --> 00:20:07,460
The emerald he seeks 
could power my wildest designs.

227
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:09,830
My genius wouldn't 
just be recognized on Earth.

228
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:12,880
It would spread virally 
to every corner of the galaxy,

229
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,130
allowing me to harness all the 
negative forces of the universe

230
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:19,380
and commune 
with Darkness itself.

231
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:22,220
Wow. That sounds big.

232
00:20:22,350 --> 00:20:25,640
It's been on my vision board for 
years. It's the Law of Attraction.

233
00:20:25,770 --> 00:20:28,560
<i>Didn't you see The Secret?</i>

234
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,690
Kaplooey!

235
00:20:30,810 --> 00:20:31,600
Kaplooey.

236
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:35,020
"Another boring night at home."

237
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:37,070
The hedgehog has returned home!

238
00:20:37,190 --> 00:20:40,320
<i>Falsa. 
Which is Latin for "wrong-o."</i>

239
00:20:40,450 --> 00:20:46,160
According to my worldwide network 
cell tower triangulation, he's lying,

240
00:20:46,290 --> 00:20:48,290
all the way

241
00:20:48,410 --> 00:20:53,080
from the majestic hinterlands 
of Eastern Siberia.

242
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:56,630
He's a long-distance liar!

243
00:20:57,670 --> 00:21:00,760
Kuh! Kuh! Kuh! 
Nga-nga-nga-nga-nga!

244
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:03,220
Yeah, there's more 
where that came from.

245
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,980
I pinpointed the coordinates. 
It's right up ahead.

246
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,820
Wow.

247
00:21:25,870 --> 00:21:27,370
Hey, Tails. Wait up.

248
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,290
Whoa.

249
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:42,260
Whoa.

250
00:21:43,630 --> 00:21:44,680
Check this out.

251
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,140
Can you translate that?

252
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:47,640
Uh, yeah.

253
00:21:48,810 --> 00:21:51,980
<i>Ages ago, 
a fearsome group of warriors,</i>

254
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,770
<i>known as the Echidnas,</i>

255
00:21:53,890 --> 00:21:55,860
<i>forged the Seven Chaos Emeralds</i>

256
00:21:55,980 --> 00:22:00,230
<i>into the most unstoppable 
weapon ever created.</i>

257
00:22:02,950 --> 00:22:04,860
The Master Emerald.

258
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:07,240
<i>With it, a single warrior</i>

259
00:22:07,370 --> 00:22:09,950
<i>could defeat entire armies.</i>

260
00:22:12,410 --> 00:22:15,330
<i>Believing no one should 
have such power,</i>

261
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:18,340
<i>an order of heroes 
recovered the Emerald</i>

262
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:21,510
<i>and swore to protect it 
from evil.</i>

263
00:22:22,340 --> 00:22:24,130
Sounds like 
the Owls and the Echidnas

264
00:22:24,260 --> 00:22:26,680
have been fighting 
each other for centuries.

265
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:32,140
Whoa.

266
00:22:41,730 --> 00:22:44,900
Wait a second. 
I've seen these symbols before.

267
00:22:48,780 --> 00:22:50,240
Here we go.

268
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:00,340
Well, that did something.

269
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:18,810
Whoa! The compass!

270
00:23:18,940 --> 00:23:20,060
This will lead us 
to the Emerald!

271
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:28,950
Hey, you got 
a little something on your...

272
00:23:29,120 --> 00:23:32,030
Oh, no. Tails, get back.

273
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:38,330
Run!

274
00:23:44,630 --> 00:23:45,670
That guy again?

275
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:47,840
Heads up, my little stalagmites.

276
00:23:47,970 --> 00:23:49,340
Someone call an Uber?

277
00:23:49,510 --> 00:23:52,930
Hey, thanks for doing 
all the hard stuff.

278
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:58,310
But we'll take it from here.

279
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:09,200
Oh! Whoo!

280
00:24:10,030 --> 00:24:12,870
Good one! 
I'm sure that wasn't important.

281
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:17,580
Tails, that's our exit. Come on.

282
00:24:30,430 --> 00:24:32,340
Uh-huh. Let's split up.

283
00:24:32,510 --> 00:24:33,550
Right.

284
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:36,060
Quick little stretch 
and here we go.

285
00:24:52,780 --> 00:24:54,280
That's new.

286
00:24:54,410 --> 00:24:56,660
Whoa.

287
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:06,960
Sonic!

288
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:20,770
Snowball fight!

289
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:38,790
Surrender the compass! 
You are no match for me.

290
00:25:44,540 --> 00:25:46,840
My rings!

291
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:53,680
Has anyone ever told you 
you've got serious anger issues?

292
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:55,840
You mock me 
with your weak jokes,

293
00:25:56,010 --> 00:25:57,890
but you know nothing 
about me, hedgehog.

294
00:25:58,010 --> 00:26:02,310
Well, I know you Echidnas have a habit of 
showing up uninvited and ruining my life.

295
00:26:06,110 --> 00:26:07,650
Sonic! Are you okay?

296
00:26:09,020 --> 00:26:12,110
Tails, take the compass 
and get out of here!

297
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:16,280
Yeah!

298
00:26:17,530 --> 00:26:19,540
Later, haters!

299
00:26:22,750 --> 00:26:24,080
Tails!

300
00:26:31,010 --> 00:26:32,380
Tails, come on. Wake up.

301
00:26:32,550 --> 00:26:35,380
He chose helping the fox 
over pursuing the compass.

302
00:26:35,550 --> 00:26:36,890
Of course he did.

303
00:26:37,010 --> 00:26:39,600
New friend, 
same pathetic weakness.

304
00:26:39,720 --> 00:26:42,140
Hmm.

305
00:26:49,730 --> 00:26:52,400
Oh, no. No, no, no. 
We're in real trouble here.

306
00:26:52,530 --> 00:26:55,950
Come on, Tails. I need you to fly 
us out of here. Time to wake up.

307
00:27:03,250 --> 00:27:06,790
See ya, kids. 
Enjoy the fresh powder.

308
00:27:31,980 --> 00:27:33,280
Did you...

309
00:27:40,740 --> 00:27:42,990
What? This better 
be important. I just...

310
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:44,120
<i>Are you skiing?</i>

311
00:27:44,450 --> 00:27:46,410
I need you to use the ring I gave 
you to save me. Like right now.

312
00:27:47,460 --> 00:27:49,790
<i>Okay, 
slow down. I don't even know where you are.</i>

313
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:52,250
You just gotta picture 
where you want the ring to go.

314
00:27:52,380 --> 00:27:53,710
So picture this.

315
00:27:56,090 --> 00:27:58,970
Oh, my God. Okay, okay. Hang on.

316
00:28:06,730 --> 00:28:08,350
What?

317
00:28:09,850 --> 00:28:11,810
<i>Did you throw it?</i>

318
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:14,270
<i>Oh, God. What? Tell me what "Oh, 
God."</i>

319
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:16,070
I mixed up the rings 
when I was teasing Jojo.

320
00:28:16,110 --> 00:28:17,860
<i>What? Where is it then?</i>

321
00:28:22,070 --> 00:28:22,700
You don't want to know.

322
00:28:22,700 --> 00:28:23,280
before I become 
a hedgehog-flavored snow cone.

323
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:25,410
Hang tight, buddy. I got this.

324
00:28:25,540 --> 00:28:27,330
With this ring, Rachel...

325
00:28:27,450 --> 00:28:29,210
Hey! Hi.

326
00:28:29,330 --> 00:28:31,210
Uh... Everything okay, bud?

327
00:28:31,330 --> 00:28:33,000
Not really. What are you doing?

328
00:28:33,130 --> 00:28:35,420
This is gonna sound crazy, 
but I need to see that ring

329
00:28:35,550 --> 00:28:37,760
for just one second. 
Have you lost your mind?

330
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:39,550
I'm gonna give it 
right back, I promise.

331
00:28:39,680 --> 00:28:42,300
Please, Randall, it's really important. No, 
bro. Go sit down.

332
00:28:42,300 --> 00:28:42,680
With this ring... Yes, baby.

333
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:44,430
I'm so sorry about this.

334
00:28:54,650 --> 00:28:56,980
Snow, my God. Oh, boy.

335
00:28:57,570 --> 00:28:59,030
Incoming!

336
00:29:03,530 --> 00:29:05,120
Oh.

337
00:29:10,540 --> 00:29:12,040
Anybody hurt?

338
00:29:12,170 --> 00:29:14,130
Sonic! Hawaii.

339
00:29:14,250 --> 00:29:15,380
Are you okay?

340
00:29:15,500 --> 00:29:17,380
What's happening? 
Are you hurt?

341
00:29:17,500 --> 00:29:19,210
No, no, I'm fine. Okay, good.

342
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:20,840
Because you're in 
so much trouble!

343
00:29:20,970 --> 00:29:23,090
Okay, you calm down.

344
00:29:23,220 --> 00:29:24,430
You talk.

345
00:29:24,550 --> 00:29:26,050
Okay, quick version.

346
00:29:26,220 --> 00:29:28,470
Robotnik is back on Earth 
and he's after a magic emerald.

347
00:29:29,980 --> 00:29:33,100
We need to get it back 
or the world is doomed.

348
00:29:33,650 --> 00:29:34,770
Tails!

349
00:29:34,900 --> 00:29:36,900
Wait! All this happened 
since yesterday?

350
00:29:37,070 --> 00:29:38,320
Wait. Who's Tails?

351
00:29:38,440 --> 00:29:39,570
Tails, can you hear me?

352
00:29:39,740 --> 00:29:41,610
Oh, Lord, 
there are two of them now.

353
00:29:41,740 --> 00:29:44,030
Okay, let me think. 
Tails, come on, buddy.

354
00:29:48,700 --> 00:29:50,040
Hey!

355
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:52,620
Randall, 
why do all of your friends have weapons?

356
00:29:53,620 --> 00:29:56,840
It's okay, everyone. 
We're federal agents.

357
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:59,880
You, too, Agent. Go ahead.

358
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:09,350
Aunt Maddie? Yeah.

359
00:30:09,470 --> 00:30:11,430
Sonic and his friend 
dropped this.

360
00:30:18,110 --> 00:30:19,110
I have an idea.

361
00:30:22,650 --> 00:30:25,450
Hey, come on. 
You can't just leave us in here.

362
00:30:25,570 --> 00:30:29,120
My friend is hurt! He needs a doctor, 
a vet, anyone!

363
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:31,660
Tails, 
you got to wake up, buddy.

364
00:30:31,790 --> 00:30:33,410
Please wake up.

365
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:42,670
All clear.

366
00:30:46,510 --> 00:30:48,180
Shh! Shh!

367
00:31:02,070 --> 00:31:03,240
We got her.

368
00:31:03,360 --> 00:31:04,990
Move in.

369
00:31:08,570 --> 00:31:09,620
Okay.

370
00:31:25,840 --> 00:31:28,010
I did not mean to do that!

371
00:31:29,890 --> 00:31:31,970
Whoo!

372
00:31:34,730 --> 00:31:36,560
Maddie! Maddie!

373
00:31:36,690 --> 00:31:38,230
We're busting out of here. 
How'd you get past the guards?

374
00:31:39,270 --> 00:31:41,190
Because that little fox 
is into some crazy stuff.

375
00:31:41,230 --> 00:31:43,610
Come on.

376
00:31:43,730 --> 00:31:45,690
Let's go. You're amazing.

377
00:32:03,880 --> 00:32:05,460
Ah.

378
00:32:33,530 --> 00:32:35,370
What's happening?

379
00:32:36,830 --> 00:32:38,620
Wait for it.

380
00:32:50,010 --> 00:32:52,470
Yes. Eureka!

381
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:55,390
I've found it!

382
00:33:13,030 --> 00:33:14,370
Sonic.

383
00:33:16,120 --> 00:33:18,660
What is that? A big problem.

384
00:33:18,790 --> 00:33:20,620
The compass led Robotnik 
to the Emerald.

385
00:33:20,750 --> 00:33:23,000
That's got to be 
hundreds of miles away.

386
00:33:24,330 --> 00:33:25,630
All right.

387
00:33:25,750 --> 00:33:27,800
Huddle up. 
Let's figure out a plan.

388
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:28,550
Together.

389
00:33:28,960 --> 00:33:30,340
I'm not letting 
anyone else get hurt

390
00:33:30,470 --> 00:33:31,590
because of me.

391
00:33:31,930 --> 00:33:33,510
I'm gonna fix this 
while I still can.

392
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:36,300
Sonic!

393
00:33:36,470 --> 00:33:38,850
Sonic, wait!

394
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:43,440
Hold on. Wait. Don't move.

395
00:33:43,560 --> 00:33:45,230
Take it easy, little guy. 
You're hurt.

396
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:49,070
But we have to help him. You 
don't know what he's up against.

397
00:34:01,330 --> 00:34:03,120
Ugh. Water.

398
00:34:03,250 --> 00:34:05,380
Why did it have to be water?

399
00:34:08,090 --> 00:34:10,960
Okay, you can do this.

400
00:34:14,470 --> 00:34:16,340
Gotta go fast.

401
00:35:45,930 --> 00:35:47,440
Oh!

402
00:35:57,490 --> 00:36:02,120
I don't want to die 
like this! It's derivative!

403
00:36:03,540 --> 00:36:05,500
Make room for Daddy!

404
00:36:13,250 --> 00:36:15,010
Two and two. Great!

405
00:36:14,210 --> 00:36:18,220
We're still bipedals, 
more or less.

406
00:36:21,090 --> 00:36:22,760
Fire in the hole!

407
00:36:24,470 --> 00:36:28,100
I've solved it. There is a 
booby trap every seven seco...

408
00:36:34,610 --> 00:36:36,570
That was a little early. Mmm.

409
00:36:36,690 --> 00:36:40,910
Oh! So glad it didn't 
cut off my mustache.

410
00:36:41,030 --> 00:36:44,120
Hey, Little Red Wrecking Ball.

411
00:36:44,240 --> 00:36:46,450
I know you're dying 
to get your Emerald on,

412
00:36:46,580 --> 00:36:51,000
but can we be a little bit more 
mindful of our surroundings?

413
00:36:51,120 --> 00:36:52,130
May I?

414
00:36:58,670 --> 00:37:01,300
<i>In 30 feet, turn left.</i>

415
00:37:01,430 --> 00:37:02,640
Work smarter, not harder.

416
00:37:24,660 --> 00:37:26,200
My pelvis.

417
00:37:30,290 --> 00:37:34,830
Okay, Secret Temple, 
let's see what you've got.

418
00:37:41,010 --> 00:37:42,680
Whoa!

419
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:44,680
No, no, no! No!

420
00:37:49,180 --> 00:37:50,230
No.

421
00:37:51,350 --> 00:37:53,310
Yes!

422
00:37:58,110 --> 00:38:00,070
<i>You have 
arrived at your destination.</i>

423
00:38:00,110 --> 00:38:03,110
Wow. That really 
opened up the space.

424
00:38:03,240 --> 00:38:06,070
I can't even picture it 
with an impenetrable wall now.

425
00:38:06,200 --> 00:38:08,580
And the rubble 
is always a nice touch.

426
00:38:17,540 --> 00:38:21,210
At last. The Master Emerald.

427
00:38:21,380 --> 00:38:22,510
Ultimate power.

428
00:38:22,630 --> 00:38:25,220
Soon order will be restored.

429
00:38:25,390 --> 00:38:28,760
All because of what 
we have done together.

430
00:38:28,890 --> 00:38:31,600
Such a lovely sentiment, 
Knuckles.

431
00:38:31,730 --> 00:38:34,640
I think I feel 
a single tear forming.

432
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,520
Sadly...

433
00:38:39,820 --> 00:38:40,940
You're as useful to me now

434
00:38:41,030 --> 00:38:44,860
as a backstage pass 
to Limp Bizkit.

435
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:46,490
Whoa, 
whoa, whoa, whoa!

436
00:38:59,090 --> 00:39:00,090
Nailed it.

437
00:39:01,340 --> 00:39:05,430
This guy is always trying 
to spoil a bad thing!

438
00:39:05,550 --> 00:39:07,180
Ah! You guys are here, too?

439
00:39:07,300 --> 00:39:07,640
Took the long way, huh?

440
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:10,760
Is everything a joke to you?

441
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:13,600
Why must you constantly 
interfere with my destiny?

442
00:39:13,730 --> 00:39:17,600
Because my destiny is to 
protect my friends and family.

443
00:39:17,730 --> 00:39:19,610
I think I just threw up 
in my mouth.

444
00:39:19,770 --> 00:39:26,110
And if you want that emerald, 
you're gonna have to go through me.

445
00:39:31,490 --> 00:39:32,950
Whoa!

446
00:39:48,090 --> 00:39:51,050
The Echidna's 
taking no prisoners today!

447
00:39:51,180 --> 00:39:55,230
Sonic has heart, 
but will he lose the quill to live?

448
00:39:56,640 --> 00:40:00,810
I don't want to fight you, 
but you're not giving me much choice.

449
00:40:05,990 --> 00:40:10,200
Too easy. Let's do this.

450
00:40:15,660 --> 00:40:17,120
Huh?

451
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:48,280
Hi there, beautiful.

452
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:51,820
You're the real deal, 
aren't you?

453
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:01,750
Say goodbye, hedgehog.

454
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:07,630
Knuckles, stop. 
Robotnik's stealing the Emerald!

455
00:41:10,010 --> 00:41:11,510
Mine.

456
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:15,180
Wait! That wasn't the deal.

457
00:41:17,390 --> 00:41:21,190
Oh, you poor, naive creature.

458
00:41:21,310 --> 00:41:23,060
It's not your fault.

459
00:41:23,190 --> 00:41:26,440
A more advanced intellect would 
have seen this move coming a mile away.

460
00:41:26,570 --> 00:41:28,690
Or 1.6 kilometers.

461
00:41:28,820 --> 00:41:31,570
But I trusted you! 
You were my friend!

462
00:41:38,620 --> 00:41:41,870
I'm sorry. 
That just hit me funny.

463
00:41:41,080 --> 00:41:44,540
Let this be 
my final lesson to you,

464
00:41:44,670 --> 00:41:47,300
you dim-witted 
celestial skin tag.

465
00:41:48,210 --> 00:41:49,300
Friends...

466
00:41:49,420 --> 00:41:53,340
are open, honest 
and vulnerable with each other.

467
00:41:53,510 --> 00:41:56,010
Which means X squared times 
the hypotenuse of Y squared,

468
00:41:56,180 --> 00:41:59,520
divided by the absolute value 
of friendship, equals...

469
00:41:59,640 --> 00:42:00,640
dookie!

470
00:42:00,730 --> 00:42:02,190
Oh, no.

471
00:42:10,240 --> 00:42:15,110
Chaos is power!

472
00:42:33,510 --> 00:42:34,300
Let's get out of here!

473
00:42:42,390 --> 00:42:45,600
That sly little fox!

474
00:42:47,770 --> 00:42:50,480
Come on, Knucklehead. 
We're not beat yet.

475
00:43:00,200 --> 00:43:02,200
Doctor, you're here.

476
00:43:03,790 --> 00:43:08,960
Yes, 
I'm here, and yet I'm...

477
00:43:10,340 --> 00:43:11,800
not all there.

478
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:13,460
Sir, are you feeling okay?

479
00:43:13,630 --> 00:43:18,300
I'm more than okay.

480
00:43:18,430 --> 00:43:21,470
I'm upgraded.

481
00:43:21,600 --> 00:43:24,560
Sinister 3.0.

482
00:43:24,680 --> 00:43:28,310
My game is next level.

483
00:43:30,360 --> 00:43:31,730
Hi.

484
00:43:34,150 --> 00:43:40,410
I can smell the electricity 
in your brain.

485
00:43:42,370 --> 00:43:44,830
You smell like a snack plate.

486
00:43:45,910 --> 00:43:49,540
Yeah, no, that's fair. 
I had a couple today.

487
00:43:49,670 --> 00:43:51,460
Sit down.

488
00:43:57,760 --> 00:43:59,640
I didn't know.

489
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:02,970
'Cause he was in the chair, 
so I didn't... Okay.

490
00:44:03,100 --> 00:44:05,270
Sir? We have a problem.

491
00:44:09,850 --> 00:44:13,900
- All teams in position! 
- Set up a perimeter!

492
00:44:14,030 --> 00:44:15,900
Move! Move! Move!

493
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:33,250
<i>Incorrectus, my trusty barnacle.</i>

494
00:44:34,500 --> 00:44:37,090
After all these years,

495
00:44:37,590 --> 00:44:39,590
what I finally got...

496
00:44:40,510 --> 00:44:42,760
is a solution.

497
00:44:53,020 --> 00:44:54,690
Commander. Status report.

498
00:44:54,820 --> 00:44:57,490
Robotnik is in there with Stone 
and a hostage. Possibly local PD.

499
00:45:09,580 --> 00:45:11,290
Um...

500
00:45:12,500 --> 00:45:14,040
Okay.

501
00:45:14,170 --> 00:45:16,840
Rockin' that new 
spring collection, I see.

502
00:45:16,960 --> 00:45:21,510
Well, if it isn't 
the Pastry King.

503
00:45:21,680 --> 00:45:23,010
The Donut Lord.

504
00:45:23,180 --> 00:45:25,050
A real genius would remember 
the name of the guy

505
00:45:25,050 --> 00:45:26,720
who helped kick your butt 
off this planet.

506
00:45:26,850 --> 00:45:28,810
And I'll do it again 
if you mess with Green Hills.

507
00:45:28,890 --> 00:45:33,690
Congratulations on your 
oh-so-temporary sense of superiority.

508
00:45:33,810 --> 00:45:36,190
You're finished, Robotnik! 
We've taken everything.

509
00:45:36,360 --> 00:45:38,860
Your lab, your drones, 
your funding!

510
00:45:38,990 --> 00:45:42,530
Let's see how big of a man you 
are without your silly little robots.

511
00:45:44,120 --> 00:45:46,280
Would you like to see how...

512
00:45:47,620 --> 00:45:49,950
big a man I can be?

513
00:46:00,630 --> 00:46:04,010
Welcome to the new norm.

514
00:46:14,020 --> 00:46:15,560
My God!

515
00:46:18,900 --> 00:46:22,740
Doctor! Take me with you!

516
00:46:46,140 --> 00:46:48,850
He's taking everything apart.

517
00:46:49,930 --> 00:46:51,470
He's building something.

518
00:46:59,270 --> 00:47:01,480
That can only be one thing.

519
00:47:01,610 --> 00:47:04,070
The fearsome power 
of the Emerald.

520
00:47:04,200 --> 00:47:06,490
If that thing really 
turns thoughts into power,

521
00:47:06,610 --> 00:47:08,240
we are in big trouble.

522
00:47:08,370 --> 00:47:09,830
Robotnik has a lot 
of bad thoughts.

523
00:47:36,810 --> 00:47:38,060
Whoa.

524
00:47:41,610 --> 00:47:44,240
Sir, you're magnificent!

525
00:47:44,360 --> 00:47:46,320
Thank you, sycophant.

526
00:47:46,450 --> 00:47:48,110
Your admiration is inevitable.

527
00:47:58,290 --> 00:48:00,460
World Domination playlist.

528
00:48:13,810 --> 00:48:15,180
Fall back.

529
00:48:16,310 --> 00:48:19,400
Fall back! Quick! Retreat!

530
00:48:24,110 --> 00:48:25,480
Sonic!

531
00:48:31,320 --> 00:48:34,700
Like a blister, 
he keeps coming back!

532
00:48:34,830 --> 00:48:37,750
He's on the okay-to-kill list. Shoot 
the missiles. Make a decision.

533
00:48:37,870 --> 00:48:40,830
I need a moment, sir. I'm 
trying to figure out how to do this.

534
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:43,000
Did you even glance at a manual?

535
00:48:43,130 --> 00:48:44,460
No! I'll do it.

536
00:48:45,500 --> 00:48:46,590
Pardon my lightning.

537
00:48:46,710 --> 00:48:49,050
You might want to 
ground yourself.

538
00:48:51,140 --> 00:48:52,140
Whoa!

539
00:48:52,220 --> 00:48:54,010
Hang on!

540
00:48:55,770 --> 00:48:57,640
Whoa!

541
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:02,440
Whoa!

542
00:49:05,110 --> 00:49:06,320
Whoo! Whoo-hoo!

543
00:49:06,480 --> 00:49:09,070
Oh, 
yeah! Whoo! Whoo-hoo-hoo! Close one.

544
00:49:09,200 --> 00:49:11,360
Sonic!

545
00:49:14,950 --> 00:49:16,660
Robotnik!

546
00:49:18,120 --> 00:49:18,790
Deceiver!

547
00:49:19,790 --> 00:49:21,620
Die, mosquito.

548
00:49:33,050 --> 00:49:35,180
Ooh! I felt that.

549
00:49:47,650 --> 00:49:50,320
Oh! Whoa!

550
00:49:54,070 --> 00:49:55,450
What just happened?

551
00:49:55,570 --> 00:49:59,160
It's the Stache Masher. 
Right here in the manual.

552
00:50:01,160 --> 00:50:02,750
Return to sender.

553
00:50:11,010 --> 00:50:12,340
Stone?

554
00:50:13,220 --> 00:50:15,050
Oh, great.

555
00:50:15,220 --> 00:50:18,350
Next thing you know, there'll be a 
report about a hostile work environment.

556
00:50:22,350 --> 00:50:24,190
Time to fight.

557
00:50:31,490 --> 00:50:32,820
We have to find his weak spot.

558
00:50:32,820 --> 00:50:34,530
Hedgehog!

559
00:50:34,660 --> 00:50:36,160
Look out!

560
00:50:42,580 --> 00:50:43,580
Let's go!

561
00:50:47,840 --> 00:50:48,880
All right, mustache.

562
00:50:49,800 --> 00:50:51,420
Come and get me.

563
00:50:51,550 --> 00:50:54,090
You don't tell me 
about coming and getting.

564
00:50:54,220 --> 00:50:56,890
I am on the cutting edge 
of coming and getting!

565
00:50:57,010 --> 00:50:58,680
Coming, getting.

566
00:50:58,800 --> 00:50:59,810
Coming, getting.

567
00:51:03,930 --> 00:51:07,440
Go! Move, guys! Move back! Let's go, 
that's it! Go, go, go!

568
00:51:07,560 --> 00:51:08,560
Keep going! Go! Go!

569
00:51:08,650 --> 00:51:10,440
No, no! Stop! Stop the truck!

570
00:51:10,610 --> 00:51:12,110
Tom, what happened here?

571
00:51:12,230 --> 00:51:14,780
You thinking what I'm 
thinking? Let's get our kid.

572
00:51:14,900 --> 00:51:16,450
We need your truck!

573
00:51:22,370 --> 00:51:25,620
Coming, 
getting. Whew!

574
00:51:25,750 --> 00:51:27,330
Yoo-hoo!

575
00:51:27,460 --> 00:51:29,170
So what's the 
plan here?

576
00:51:29,290 --> 00:51:30,130
Huh?

577
00:51:30,290 --> 00:51:32,000
You gonna build 
a big robot house?

578
00:51:32,130 --> 00:51:34,470
Get yourself a big robot wife?

579
00:51:34,590 --> 00:51:38,970
I'm going to enslave humanity and 
force them to service my machines.

580
00:51:39,140 --> 00:51:41,930
First, Green Hills. 
Then the universe.

581
00:51:42,060 --> 00:51:43,310
Then the multiverse.

582
00:51:43,430 --> 00:51:46,310
Then who knows? 
Maybe that'll be enough.

583
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:48,310
Full disclosure?

584
00:51:48,980 --> 00:51:51,860
You won't be there.

585
00:52:08,540 --> 00:52:10,750
Snot rocket!

586
00:52:12,170 --> 00:52:13,250
No, no, no!

587
00:52:19,760 --> 00:52:22,760
Giving up already?

588
00:52:22,890 --> 00:52:27,100
Not so tough when you're fighting 
someone 700 times your size, are ya?

589
00:52:28,980 --> 00:52:31,480
You can't beat me!

590
00:52:31,610 --> 00:52:34,980
I'm all-powerful! All-knowing!

591
00:52:37,530 --> 00:52:39,950
All-seeing.

592
00:52:40,820 --> 00:52:42,990
Looks like your fancy robot 
has a glitch.

593
00:52:43,160 --> 00:52:45,370
Is it me? 
What about me? I'm over here.

594
00:52:45,370 --> 00:52:47,200
Up top! Down below! 
Behind you!

595
00:52:47,330 --> 00:52:49,420
I'm 
over here. Sorry! Over here.

596
00:52:49,540 --> 00:52:51,080
Too slow! Try again.

597
00:52:51,210 --> 00:52:53,380
You can't outsmart me. 
Missed me again.

598
00:52:53,500 --> 00:52:54,500
I'm the outsmarter-er!

599
00:52:56,340 --> 00:52:58,130
Robotnik!

600
00:52:58,260 --> 00:53:01,010
I am also a hologram.

601
00:53:01,140 --> 00:53:03,010
Disloyal.

602
00:53:03,140 --> 00:53:06,020
"Dis" is how I roll.

603
00:53:34,340 --> 00:53:36,000
Where's my Emerald?

604
00:53:36,590 --> 00:53:38,380
No, no, no, no!

605
00:53:38,550 --> 00:53:41,050
Computer, auxiliary power.

606
00:53:43,260 --> 00:53:45,220
Move, you hunk of junk!

607
00:54:12,870 --> 00:54:13,920
Come on.

608
00:54:16,000 --> 00:54:18,380
There he is! Go! Go, go, go!

609
00:54:27,100 --> 00:54:28,100
No!

610
00:54:28,180 --> 00:54:29,640
We got you, Sonic.

611
00:54:30,810 --> 00:54:32,350
Hold on!

612
00:54:45,320 --> 00:54:47,740
- You guys okay? 
- Yeah.

613
00:54:49,120 --> 00:54:50,830
Okay.

614
00:54:55,580 --> 00:54:57,540
I got the Emerald. 
We could still defeat him.

615
00:54:57,670 --> 00:55:00,960
Come on, come on. How does 
this thing work? What do I do?

616
00:55:02,170 --> 00:55:03,920
What?

617
00:55:04,050 --> 00:55:06,840
No. No, no, no!

618
00:55:10,510 --> 00:55:14,890
Look at the happy little family.

619
00:55:28,870 --> 00:55:30,450
No!

620
00:55:32,290 --> 00:55:34,330
I got him!

621
00:55:34,460 --> 00:55:39,380
I finally got him!

622
00:55:43,510 --> 00:55:45,550
What was that?

623
00:56:31,220 --> 00:56:33,140
It's over, Eggman.

624
00:56:33,260 --> 00:56:37,810
I like the 
new look. It works for you.

625
00:56:37,940 --> 00:56:39,940
What do you say 
we just let bygones be bygones?

626
00:56:41,020 --> 00:56:41,940
I did some things, 
you did some things.

627
00:56:42,980 --> 00:56:45,030
There are good people 
on both sides.

628
00:56:46,570 --> 00:56:49,860
Surely two intelligent beings

629
00:56:51,450 --> 00:56:53,700
can work these things out!

630
00:57:04,550 --> 00:57:06,460
Come on, buddy.

631
00:57:06,550 --> 00:57:07,970
Get him, Sonic! Come on.

632
00:57:08,090 --> 00:57:09,590
Yeah. Come on.

633
00:57:25,820 --> 00:57:27,610
It's like that?

634
00:57:28,780 --> 00:57:31,450
Okay, we're not friends.

635
00:57:35,580 --> 00:57:38,040
Later, hater!

636
00:57:49,300 --> 00:57:50,800
Sonic! Buddy!

637
00:58:08,730 --> 00:58:09,860
Mmm.

638
00:58:10,030 --> 00:58:11,110
Oh, you got to try this.

639
00:58:12,240 --> 00:58:13,780
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

640
00:58:22,120 --> 00:58:23,870
Sonic! Whoa!

641
00:58:25,420 --> 00:58:27,340
Bring it in, bud.

642
00:58:28,460 --> 00:58:30,170
It's good to be back in blue.

643
00:58:37,470 --> 00:58:39,100
Whoa! You fixed it.

644
00:58:39,220 --> 00:58:42,600
I've spent my whole life 
questing for this.

645
00:58:42,770 --> 00:58:43,940
Now I have it.

646
00:58:44,060 --> 00:58:45,810
Now we have it.

647
00:58:45,940 --> 00:58:50,730
We must make a vow to use our 
powers to keep the universe safe,

648
00:58:50,820 --> 00:58:51,820
Oh, I know!

649
00:58:51,990 --> 00:58:53,200
A power bump!

650
00:58:53,320 --> 00:58:54,990
Good idea.

651
00:58:55,160 --> 00:58:58,660
It's an Earth custom. 
An unbreakable promise.

652
00:58:58,780 --> 00:59:00,660
Very well.

653
00:59:01,250 --> 00:59:03,830
A power bump it is.

654
00:59:04,920 --> 00:59:06,670
Power bump!

655
00:59:10,380 --> 00:59:12,130
It's truly a beautiful day

656
00:59:12,260 --> 00:59:14,420
for baseball here 
in Green Hills.

657
00:59:14,550 --> 00:59:16,260
An exciting lineup today

658
00:59:16,390 --> 00:59:19,550
with the debut appearance 
of two new players!

659
00:59:19,680 --> 00:59:23,980
On the mound, 
rookie sensation from across the galaxy,

660
00:59:24,100 --> 00:59:26,480
Miles "Tails" Prower,

661
00:59:26,600 --> 00:59:31,780
facing off against the powerhouse, 
Knuckles the Echidna.

662
00:59:31,940 --> 00:59:33,190
Don't think about it too much.

663
00:59:33,320 --> 00:59:35,200
Just keep your elbow up, 
eye on the ball

664
00:59:35,360 --> 00:59:36,530
and give it a ride.

665
00:59:40,780 --> 00:59:42,240
Power bump!

666
00:59:46,580 --> 00:59:48,750
Ha! Victory is mine!

667
00:59:48,880 --> 00:59:51,460
Hey, no fair! 
That shouldn't count.

668
00:59:51,590 --> 00:59:53,710
First base is also mine!

669
00:59:53,880 --> 00:59:55,550
I think that was our 
only ball.

670
00:59:55,720 --> 00:59:57,680
I have conquered 
the second of the bases!

671
00:59:57,680 --> 00:59:59,970
Who wants ice cream?

672
01:00:00,100 --> 01:00:01,390
Knocked the cover off that.

673
01:00:01,560 --> 01:00:03,850
Ice cream! Ice cream, yeah!

674
01:00:04,060 --> 01:00:06,390
I'm proud of our little guy.

675
01:00:06,520 --> 01:00:10,020
I really like his new friends, 
especially the red one.

676
01:00:10,150 --> 01:00:12,770
He cracks me up. 
Heck of a swing too.

677
01:00:12,900 --> 01:00:14,070
Come on, fox.

678
01:00:14,190 --> 01:00:15,820
Our dessert adventure 
awaits. Whoo!

679
01:00:15,940 --> 01:00:16,990
Good job, guys. Yeah.

680
01:00:17,110 --> 01:00:18,410
You too, baby.

681
01:00:18,570 --> 01:00:21,370
Let's go get some ice cream. 
Come on, come on.

682
01:00:21,490 --> 01:00:23,740
I'm happy for you, pal.

683
01:00:23,910 --> 01:00:25,290
Got your wingmen.

684
01:00:25,410 --> 01:00:26,750
Perfect friends to grow up with.

685
01:00:26,910 --> 01:00:30,580
Come on, 
Knuckles. Ah! My victory chariot!

686
01:00:33,300 --> 01:00:34,800
Race you to the truck.

687
01:00:36,300 --> 01:00:37,550
One, two, three, go!

688
01:00:37,670 --> 01:00:40,140
No, don't go easy on me. 
I want your best.

689
01:00:40,260 --> 01:00:43,140
Sonic, I have just been told 
they have sprinkles.

690
01:00:43,310 --> 01:00:46,980
Ice cream and sprinkles? 
This is your new destiny.

691
01:00:47,100 --> 01:00:51,980
What a perfect meal to celebrate 
my victory over you in base of ball.

692
01:00:52,110 --> 01:00:54,820
What? I mean, 
you barely beat me.

693
01:00:54,940 --> 01:00:58,150
Ha! You've never been 
beaten so hard.

694
01:02:32,910 --> 01:02:34,540
Agent, I want an update.

695
01:02:34,670 --> 01:02:37,750
Still searching, 
sir. We haven't found any sign of Robotnik.

696
01:02:37,880 --> 01:02:40,090
No one could've 
survived that crash.

697
01:02:40,260 --> 01:02:43,430
He's toast. Good riddance.

698
01:02:43,550 --> 01:02:46,680
What a mess that lunatic made.

699
01:02:46,800 --> 01:02:49,430
Sir, there's something else.

700
01:02:49,600 --> 01:02:53,480
When we were wiping Robotnik off 
our database, we found something.

701
01:02:53,600 --> 01:02:56,690
A file buried deep in our system 
and dating back over 50 years.

702
01:02:57,690 --> 01:02:59,230
What was it?

703
01:02:59,360 --> 01:02:59,650
Coordinates, sir.

704
01:03:00,690 --> 01:03:02,530
Coordinates? To what?

705
01:03:02,650 --> 01:03:05,740
<i>A secret research facility.</i>

706
01:03:05,860 --> 01:03:07,990
<i>It was a black site, sir.</i>

707
01:03:08,120 --> 01:03:10,950
<i>Someone worked very hard 
to keep this hidden.</i>

708
01:03:11,100 --> 01:03:13,410
<i>My God.</i>

709
01:03:14,330 --> 01:03:15,830
<i>Project Shadow.</i>
